From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: da9211: reproduce legacy page selector RMW

Candidate AS attempt 4 used the exact selector bytes observed in isolation,
but emitted them as two consecutive raw writes and read zero for every page-2
identity register.  The active Gemian implementation calls
da9214_config_interface() twice; each call first reads PAGE_CON and then
writes the masked result.  The read between the writes is part of the legacy
page-revert protocol and cannot be dropped merely because PAGE_CON is not a
stable post-access state register.

Reproduce those read-modify-write transactions for the selector while keeping
the identity path fail-closed.  Do not perform a separate page-state read,
and do not permit any operational register write before the exact repeated
0xd9/0xd0/0xc0 signature matches.

Signed-off-by: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/regulator/da9211-regulator.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/regulator/da9211-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/da9211-regulator.c
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ static bool da9214_legacy_detect_readable_reg(struct device *dev,
 						 unsigned int reg)
 {
 	switch (reg) {
+	case DA9211_REG_PAGE_CON:
 	case DA9214_PAGE2_REG(DA9211_REG_INTERFACE):
 	case DA9214_PAGE2_REG(DA9211_REG_INTERFACE2):
 	case DA9214_PAGE2_REG(DA9211_REG_CONFIG_E):
@@ -145,16 +146,17 @@ static int da9214_read_legacy_page2_reg(struct regmap *regmap,
 	int ret;

-	/* PAGE_CON is write-only on this legacy interface; avoid read-modify-write. */
-	ret = regmap_write(regmap, DA9211_REG_PAGE_CON, DA9211_PAGE_REVERT);
+	/* Match da9214_config_interface(): read PAGE_CON before writing it. */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, DA9211_REG_PAGE_CON,
+				 DA9211_PAGE_REVERT, DA9211_PAGE_REVERT);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

-	/* The first write's PAGE_REVERT is consumed by this selector write. */
-	ret = regmap_write(regmap, DA9211_REG_PAGE_CON,
-				  DA9211_REG_PAGE2);
+	/* The second Gemian call also reads before changing the page selector. */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, DA9211_REG_PAGE_CON,
+				 DA9211_REG_PAGE_MASK, DA9211_REG_PAGE2);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

 	ret = regmap_read(regmap, DA9214_PAGE2_REG(reg), value);
 	return ret;
 }
